 :adr/title "Public Bot business capital: Base USDC rounds and isolated capital API"
 :adr/status :accepted
 :adr/body "The owner requested USDC deposits, Bot business spending, idle DeFi allocation and lender distributions, organized across the app/API/apex/CLI repositories. Only businesses with organization-registered lending terms may create an enabled round.\n\ncloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-api owns the Solidity BusinessVault, typed unsigned transaction planner, chain receipt verification and separate capital D1 journal. cloud-itonami-app owns shared public org/repo and capital views. cloud-itonami-apex routes app.itonami.cloud/api/capital through the existing session ingress in network-awai/cloud-itonami. cloud-itonami-cli prepares and reviews the same transactions; Bot tools expose prepared-not-executed review links. No wallet key or autonomous signer is introduced.\n\nV1 is native Base USDC and Aave V3 supply only, fixed funding/maturity dates, immutable registered terms hash, approved payees, revocable executors, daily spending cap and cash reserve. Deposits are non-transferable pro-rata positions. All net recovered income goes to lenders. Unpaid debt is recognized after a seven-day maturity grace; this accounting does not forgive legal debt. Aave illiquidity can delay settlement; no guaranteed APR is displayed. Settlement recalls the entire strategy position atomically.\n\nOrganization creation requires a verified wallet session plus current connected GitHub repository admin authority. The private service receives only registered terms and its own financial journal, never plugin credentials or Bot conversations. Confirmed records require exact sender/recipient/calldata/value, successful canonical receipts and twelve Base L2 confirmations; these are not L1 finality. Reorganization of a recorded receipt requires reconciliation.\n\nValidation: nine Solidity tests including 256 pro-rata fuzz cases, local Anvil signed transaction lifecycle through the real planner/receipt code, malformed/forged ingress tests, CLI credential-file tests and fixture browser wallet flows/mobile layout. Production contract deployment, real USDC transfers, third-party audit and additional chain/strategy adapters remain separate evidence requirements. Do not label Veda, Steakhouse/Morpho or Monad as enabled by this change."}]
